MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The funnel ended at `checkout_created`. Stripe's success_url returned the buyer
to /?paid=1&session_id=cs_... and NOTHING on either side of the wire read it:
no confirmation screen, no customer email, no endpoint that could resolve the
session id. A customer paid and landed on the marketing homepage as if they had
never clicked. The webhook mailed the operator only.

This ships the missing two arrows of `webhook -> fulfillment -> confirmation`.

- shared/pilot-order.ts (new): PILOT_OFFER_FULFILLMENT (deliverable + intake
  checklist per tier) and toPilotOrder(), a pure Stripe-session -> safe public
  projection mapper. No Stripe SDK import: this module ships to the browser.
- shared/schema.ts: PilotOrder / PilotOrderStatus wire schemas.
- server: GET /api/pilot-order/:sessionId (rate-limited, format-checked,
  no-store, safe projection only). Webhook now also handles
  checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded and sends the CUSTOMER a German
  confirmation stating package, reference, deliverable and the exact project
  data needed to start. Send is guarded per session so SEPA's second event
  cannot double-mail; a failed send escalates to the operator instead of
  vanishing into a log line. sendNotificationEmail generalised to sendEmail.
- client: getPilotOrder() + <PilotConfirmation/>, mounted in #pilot-start.
  Renders nothing without the checkout params, so every other visitor is
  unaffected. Handles ?canceled=1 and cleans the URL after reading.
- SEPA correctness: session.status and payment_status are mapped to four
  distinct states. A completed-but-unsettled SEPA debit reads as "processing",
  not as a failure, because checkout enables sepa_debit.
- No invented turnaround. The AGB states none, so responseWindow renders only
  from ET_PILOT_RESPONSE_WINDOW.

Also fixes two verification gaps found on the way:
- package.json had NO test script. vitest and 18 engine tests existed and never
  ran before a deploy. Adds test / test:watch / verify.
- `check` only ran the root tsconfig, so server + api type errors shipped
  unchecked (the tsconfig comment even says so). Now runs both projects.
- .env.example: LEAD_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL no longer a personal Gmail.

Evidence: pnpm check clean (both projects), 37/37 vitest (19 new), pnpm build
clean, smoke-test 13/13 against the production bundle.

